CommitDate: Fri Sep 25 08:03:58 2026 -0500

    fix: AUG-075 check/recall fail closed on a dead substrate
    
    recall() collapsed every non-200 response — including _req's st=0 transport
    contract — into the same [] a genuinely empty store returns, so `check`
    answered "no stored evidence matched — treat as a new question" (rc=0) while
    the evidence sat in an unreachable store, and `recall` printed nothing at all.
    recall() now raises the new SubstrateError (a SystemExit subclass, so any
    uncaught raise stays a clean CLI failure) for st=0 and every non-200, while a
    real 200 keeps returning [] so an empty store may be believed. cmd_check and
    cmd_recall catch it, print the substrate's own words with an explicit
    fail-closed note, and exit 1; cmd_ask and gate_question (the other recall
    callers) map the same raise onto their existing fail-closed channels so a dead
    substrate can never read as "no evidence" there either. The sibling walk keeps
    its documented SPEC-002 2.1 tolerance via recall's missing_ok carve-out: a
    404 from a never-started sibling namespace is still "no rows here", but a
    substrate that cannot answer is an error everywhere. The _req transport
    contract and its inline 429 retries are untouched; every case is pinned at the
    db() boundary so the no-bypass property holds.
